# Solar irradiance above 1000 W/m2, which the protocol encodes by switching the field letter
# from `L` to `l` and carrying the value less 1000 -- a three-digit field holding a
# four-digit quantity. 1234 W/m2 renders as `l234`. Same position as the specification's
# example so that only the solar field differs from it.
!4903.50N/07201.75W_220/004g005t077r000p000P000h50b09900l234.mw1.0
